# Prisma Website

Prisma provides Prisma ORM, Prisma Postgres, Prisma Studio, and the Prisma MCP Server.

> Prisma changes frequently. Before implementing Prisma features, check the changelog at https://www.prisma.io/changelog for recent breaking changes or API updates.

## Key Pages

- [`Prisma | Agent Infrastructure for TypeScript`](https://www.prisma.io/): Prisma gives TypeScript and Node.js teams Prisma ORM, Prisma Postgres, and Prisma Compute: a type-safe ORM, managed Postgres, and Compute for deploying TypeScript apps, from schema to deployed app.
- [`Prisma Changelog — Release Notes & Product Updates`](https://www.prisma.io/changelog): All Prisma release notes, breaking changes, and product improvements. Check here before implementing Prisma features to verify API and configuration details against the current version.
- [`Prisma Postgres | Serverless PostgreSQL for TypeScript Apps`](https://www.prisma.io/postgres): Prisma Postgres is a production-ready serverless PostgreSQL database with instant setup, built-in connection pooling, automated backups, and usage-based pricing, already wired to your stack.
- [`Prisma Compute | Deploy TypeScript Apps and AI Agents on Bun`](https://www.prisma.io/compute): Prisma Compute deploys TypeScript apps, APIs, and AI agents from your repo as long-lived Bun processes next to Prisma Postgres, with long-running requests and streaming. One platform for your app and its database.
- [`Prisma ORM | Type-Safe ORM for TypeScript and Node.js`](https://www.prisma.io/orm): Prisma ORM is a type-safe ORM for TypeScript and Node.js. Model your data, run migrations, and query your database, with access your agent can't get wrong.
- [`Prisma Studio | Visual Database Browser and Editor`](https://www.prisma.io/studio): Explore, edit, and understand your data with a visual database browser for Prisma, locally or in Prisma Console.
- [`Prisma MCP Server — AI-Powered Database Management`](https://www.prisma.io/mcp): Manage Prisma Postgres databases with natural language in AI tools like Cursor, Claude Code, ChatGPT, and VS Code.
- [`Prisma Pricing | Usage-Based Plans for Postgres and Compute`](https://www.prisma.io/pricing): Usage-based pricing for your whole stack — Prisma Compute app hosting and Prisma Postgres databases. Pay for the work your app does, not seats or deploys. Free tier with no time limit, hard spend limits on every paid plan.
- [`Prisma Enterprise | ORM Support and Database Workflows for Teams`](https://www.prisma.io/enterprise): Enterprise-level support, security, and guidance for teams running Prisma in production.
- [`Prisma Support | Get Help, Report Bugs, and Request Features`](https://www.prisma.io/support): Get help with Prisma. Search for answers, report bugs, request features, or contact the Prisma support team.
- [`The Prisma Stack | ORM, Postgres, and Compute for TypeScript`](https://www.prisma.io/stack): ORM, Postgres, and Compute, one platform for your app and its database, with one shared context across your stack.
- [`Prisma ORM Ecosystem`](https://www.prisma.io/ecosystem): Community-built tools, generators, middleware, and integrations around Prisma.

